<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Radegast 1996 audited net rises.</title>
<headline>Czech Radegast 1996 audited net rises.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech brewer Pivovar Radegast a.s., one third owned by Britain's Bass plc, posted audited 1996 after-tax profit of 140 million crowns compared with 96 million in 1995, filings with the Prague Stock Exchange showed on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>					 1996		  1995</p>
<p>total assests (CZK million)     3,939.277	   2,646.934</p>
<p>current assets		  1,490.048	     478.819</p>
<p>paid-in capital		 1,662.563	   1,603.263</p>
<p>basic equity			794.320	     794.320</p>
<p>foreign sources		 2,185.031	   1,025.045</p>
<p>sales of external goods	 101.749		50.232</p>
<p>production			1,577.946	   1,353.743</p>
<p>sales of own goods/services 1,554.150	   1,343.143</p>
<p>writeoffs			   185.329	     145.269</p>
<p>turover in investment prop.    95.843		 N/A</p>
<p>operating result		  305.638	     219.680</p>
<p>income tax			   94.720	     103.181</p>
<p>profit on ordinary activities 140.914		92.815</p>
<p>extraordinary income tax	  1.310		 2.561</p>
<p>net result after-tax	    140.008		95.776</p>
<p>pre-tax result		    236.038	     201.518</p>
<p>Note. Results are according to Czech accounting standards. he company has scheduled its annual general meeting for June 19.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
